# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project has no dependencies, no build step and no generated output, so
# there is very little to exclude. Everything here is either an operating
# system artefact or an editor's private state — nothing that belongs to the
# site itself.
#
# Note in particular what is NOT ignored: assets/img is committed. It is around
# 11 MB of ordinary photographs, which git handles comfortably, and the site
# does not work without them.
# =============================================================================

# --- Windows ---
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Sync artefacts ---
# The project used to live inside OneDrive, which left these behind. It has
# been moved out since, but the rules cost nothing and other sync clients
# leave the same litter.
*.tmp
~$*

# --- macOS, in case the project is ever opened there ---
.DS_Store
._*

# --- Editors ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Logs ---
# The local dev server can be started with its output redirected to a file.
*.log
dev/*.log

# =============================================================================
# NOTHING BELOW EXISTS IN THIS PROJECT YET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The entries above cover what is actually here today. These cover what would
# arrive the day a backend is connected, and they are written in advance on
# purpose: the first commit after adding a real service is exactly when a
# credential file gets swept up by a hurried `git add -A`, and a secret that
# has been pushed once has to be treated as leaked even after it is deleted.
#
# Git only ignores files it is not already tracking, so adding these now costs
# nothing and cannot change what is committed today.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets ---
# Any key, token or service-account credential belongs on a server and never
# in this repository. See the security note at the top of
# data/admin/admin-repo.js.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
serviceAccount*.json
*-service-account.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
secrets.json
credentials.json

# --- Dependencies and build output ---
# The site is deliberately dependency-free and has no build step. If either
# ever changes, the installed tree and the generated output are not source.
node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.*
dist/
build/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/

# --- Hosting and tooling state ---
.vercel/
.netlify/
.firebase/
.wrangler/
coverage/
